From: pas7std co-op <coop@pas7std.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 0009/0010] native NPC store: stop re-cloning and re-stringifying the whole root on every read

A live V8 CPU profile of the running server (1 ms sampling, ~21 000 samples per
25 s, ~100 NPCs) attributed 62.7% of self time to cloneValue and 24.0% to
ensureRootShape in server/src/space/npc/nativeNpcStore.js. Every readCollection,
writeCollectionRow and removeCollectionRow re-read the entire NPC root (entities,
modules, cargo, wrecks for every system), deep-cloned it twice through
JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) and compared two full JSON.stringify results.

Rows are only ever written through subpaths (`/<collection>/<rowID>`), so the
default root keys cannot disappear after the first verification. The root shape is
now verified once per table per process (rootShapeVerified + rootShapeReady), and
readCollection reads only the collection it was asked for.

Note for reviewers: the memo line `rootShapeVerified.add(tableName)` is what makes
the cache work at all; without it the function still takes the cold path and the
cost stays. tests/coop-native-npc-store-patch.test.mjs asserts it.
